  "worked_solution": "A quadrilateral has $n=4$ sides. Therefore, the sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral must be \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding up the internal angles and solving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠O+m∠M+m∠N+m∠P & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {93}^{∘}+(14x-{7}^{∘})+(11x-{2}^{∘})+{76}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 25x+{160}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 25x & ={200}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={8}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
